==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkɒkl̩/}}
* {{rhymes|ɒkəl}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|coquille||lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|VL.}} {{recons|cocchilia|lang=VL.}}, form of {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|conchylia|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|κογχύλιον||tr=konkhylion|lang=grc}}, diminutive of {{term|lang=grc|κογχύλη||tr=konkhylès|mussel}}.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various [[edible]] [[European]] [[bivalve]] [[mollusk]]s, of the [[family]] ''[[Cardiidae]]'', having [[heart]]-[[shaped]] [[shell]]s.
# The [[shell]] of such cockle.
# {{context|plural}} One’s [[innermost]] [[feeling]]s (only in the expression “[[warm the cockles of one's heart|the cockles of one’s heart]]”).
# {{context|directly from French coquille}} A [[wrinkle]], [[pucker]]
# ''hence'' A defect in [[sheepskin]]; firm dark [[nodule]]s caused by the bites of [[ked]]s on live sheep

